WEBVTT

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.480
Creatives, stop making thumbnails by hand.

00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:05.100
In Adobe Firefly, there's a quick action for that.

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:11.100
More and more, we see that tools need to work hard for you.

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:13.299
And Firefly Quick Actions does just that,

00:00:13.299 --> 00:00:15.520
by simplifying and speeding up your workflows.

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:19.160
Honestly, thumbnails used to eat my whole afternoon.

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:22.695
So now, not only can you do more things by yourself,

00:00:22.695 --> 00:00:25.040
you can do them quickly in one place.

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:27.595
Generate thumbnails, build product ads,

00:00:27.595 --> 00:00:31.000
upscale images, and enhance audio right inside Firefly.

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:34.840
Next up, building a story in Firefly Video.

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:39.160
Now, it is easy to turn your idea into a plan.

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:43.063
The assistant in Firefly Video helps develop story arcs,

00:00:43.063 --> 00:00:45.440
scenes, and shots for standout videos.

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:49.316
It keeps my locations, characters, and objects consistent,

00:00:49.316 --> 00:00:52.120
and I still get the final say on every shot.

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:54.818
Then edit it all in Firefly Video.

00:00:54.818 --> 00:00:57.320
It's video editing made drag and drop easy.

00:00:57.620 --> 00:00:59.820
A simplified timeline lets anyone

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:02.020
arrange, preview, and edit clips.

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:07.074
It is perfect for turning my product shots into a reel with a quick action,

00:01:07.074 --> 00:01:10.320
then reworking the clips for my channel that night.

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:14.280
And last, with Firefly Image, you can adjust any part of your picture.

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:18.460
With Edit Object, select any object and edit it on its own.

00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:22.023
Restyle it with a prompt or swap it with a reference image,

00:01:22.023 --> 00:01:24.560
and the rest of the scene stays untouched.

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:28.260
So if it's just a jacket that looks off, you fix just the jacket.

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:30.060
So which one are you opening tomorrow?

00:01:30.260 --> 00:01:31.380
All of them, in a row.

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:34.412
Take a video you generated with a quick action,

00:01:34.412 --> 00:01:37.120
then trim, reorder, or regenerate any frame.

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:38.420
All in Firefly.

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:39.600
And that's the update.

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:42.820
Try it all at firefly.adobe.com.
